@*
    The quiet placeholder for every moment the application is busy with something a reader did not
    ask to watch: working out who is signed in, dressing the welcome deck, and each leg of the
    sign-in and sign-out round trip.

    It exists because the alternative is what the framework does by default — "Checking login
    state...", "Completing login...", "Processing logout" — a line of small text in the top-left
    corner of an otherwise empty page. Each is a different sentence about the same thing, which is
    "wait a moment", and none of them is anything a reader can act on. One shape, centred, saying
    the same thing without words, is less to look at and less to read.

    It is a copy of wwwroot/index.html's boot screen, down to the progress bar, and that is the
    whole point of it. The runtime hands over partway through the wait, and anything that does not
    match exactly reads as a second screen — the bar disappearing and four bars alone appearing in
    its place, which is what this looked like before. Matching it means the handover is invisible:
    one loading screen from the first paint to the welcome, however many components drew it.

    KEEP IN STEP with the #app markup in wwwroot/index.html.
*@

<div class="splash splash--settling">
    @*
        All three waits are drawn and app.css shows the one index.html's script picked on the first
        paint — which is why the pick is made there and not here. It is one answer for the whole
        visit, so this screen and the runtime's are always wearing the same shape, and the handover
        stays invisible however many times a Settling is drawn.
    *@
    <div class="splash__book" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="splash__page splash__page--left"></div>
        <div class="splash__page splash__page--right"></div>
        <div class="splash__leaf"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="splash__stack" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="splash__stack-book"></div>
        <div class="splash__stack-book"></div>
        <div class="splash__stack-book"></div>
        <div class="splash__stack-book"></div>
        <div class="splash__stack-book"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="splash__reader" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="splash__screen">
            <div class="splash__line"></div>
            <div class="splash__line"></div>
            <div class="splash__line"></div>
            <div class="splash__line"></div>
            <div class="splash__line"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="splash__title">ReadingTracker</p>
    @*
        The runtime stops updating --blazor-load-percentage once it has handed over, so by here it
        is at 100% and stays there: the bar arrives full and holds, rather than restarting or
        vanishing. The fallback is 100% rather than the boot screen's sliver for the same reason —
        whatever is being waited for now, downloading the application is not it.
    *@
    <div class="splash__track" role="progressbar" aria-label="Loading ReadingTracker">
        <div class="splash__fill splash__fill--settled"></div>
    </div>
    <span class="visually-hidden" role="status">Loading</span>
</div>
